{
 "recipe": {
  "title": "Gated garden: checking a level in each of its states",
  "summary": "A courtyard, a gate that stays shut until you carry the key to it, and a garden behind the gate. `phases` names the states a rule creates (`gate_open`: the `open_gate` rule has fired), so `lint`, `reach`, `walk` and `verify` can check the garden is sealed at first AND walkable afterwards, instead of calling it unreachable.",
  "teaches": [
   "`phases`: {name: [rule ids assumed fired]}; what those rules open (`deactivate`, `collision`) is open to the analysis tools in that phase",
   "`checks.reach[].phase` and `checks.walk[].phase` test one state; `\"reachable\": false` asserts a place is still cut off",
   "`lint` runs every phase and drops an `unreachable`/`zone`/`floor` finding that some phase resolves",
   "`red_engine2 reach|lint|walk|plan --phase gate_open` looks at one state by hand"
  ],
  "tips": [
   "The initial state is implicit (`initial`): the unconditional `start` rules apply there. Name a phase for each state worth proving.",
   "Phases do not change the game: `checks.sim` plays the real rules, so keep a scenario that really opens the gate."
  ]
 },
